		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: TYT MD-UV380/390 / RT-3S / DM1701 Installation information]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2380&amp;p=37265#p37265"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>For a MD-UV390, the OpenGD77 firmware installation instructions state one should use donor firmware MD9600-CSV(2571V5)-V26.45.bin. The official MD9600 V5 firmware contains both MD9600-CSV(2571V5)-V26.45.bin and MD9600-CSV-GPS(2571V5)-P26.45.bin. The MD-UV390 being upgraded has GPS. Should one use MD9600-CSV-GPS(2571V5)-P26.45.bin, or use MD9600-CSV(2571V5)-V26.45.bin, as stated in the instructions?</div></blockquote>Always MD9600-CSV(2571V5)-V26.45.bin , this file is only used for extracting the DMR codec, nothing else.<br>Everything else is made with code made for OpenGD77.</div></blockquote>Just to clarify... We do not extract the codec.<br><br>We patch the official firmware and replace the UI and other functionality with OpenGD77 and leave the codec exactly as it is.<br><br>We can't extract the codec for legal reasons.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed May 28, 2025 10:55 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
